.TH "conquest-tty" 6 "" ""
.SH NAME
conquest-tty \- Conquest curses (text terminal) client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBconquest-tty\fP [OPTIONS]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBconquest-tty\fP is the curses client for Conquest, a multi-player,
real-time space combat game.  It plays in any text terminal of at
least 80 columns by 25 lines, including over ssh, and talks to the
same \fBconquestd\fP(6) servers as the OpenGL client \fBconquest\fP(6).
.PP
The object of the game is twofold.  The short-range goal is to
accumulate "kills" by shooting down enemy players.  The long-range
goal is to conquer the universe for your team by taking every
\fIcore\fP planet.  You take planets by killing off the enemy's armies
via bombardment, and then beaming your team's armies down.
.PP
Your options and log file are kept in ~/.conquest/, or in the
directory named by the \fICONQUEST_USERDIR\fP environment variable.
.PP
Inside the game, type \fBh\fP for a list of commands.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
If neither \fI\-s\fP nor \fI\-m\fP is given, the client connects to
a server on your own host at port 1701.
.TP 8
.B \-s <server[:port]>
Connect to the server running on \fIserver\fP port \fIport\fP.  The
default port is 1701.
.TP 8
.B \-m
Query the metaserver and provide a list of servers to choose from.
.TP 8
.B \-M <metaserver>
Specify an alternate metaserver.
.TP 8
.B \-u
Do not attempt to use UDP for the motion data from the server.
.TP 8
.B \-v
Be more verbose in the log file.  More \-v's increase verbosity.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
